259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (Overall, this project demonstrates how technology can be leveraged to combat the dual problems of food wastage and hunger. It provides a practical, scalable model for communities to adopt, harnessing the power of web-based systems to facilitate social good. The Food Waste Management System contributes not only to efficient resource utilization but also supports sustainability and social welfare in the broader context.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (The platform uses PHP on the backend and MySQL for data management, ensuring secure user authentication, real-time status updates, and centralized tracking of all operations. Delivery agents are assigned donation pickups and drop-offs, updating the system at each step to maintain transparency and traceability. By offering distinct interfaces and workflows for users, admins, and delivery staff, the solution minimizes operational errors and optimizes the end-to-end donation process.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (Food waste is a critical concern with significant social, environmental, and economic repercussions. Large quantities of edible food are discarded daily, even as millions struggle with hunger and malnutrition. Addressing this gap requires not only social awareness but also practical technological interventions that enable surplus food to reach those in need efficiently. The Food Waste Management System project was developed in response to this challenge, aiming to connect food donors with beneficiaries through an accessible and robust online platform.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
