/E (Food waste remains one of the most pressing concerns facing societies around the world, particularly in developing nations where hunger and malnutrition persist alongside large amounts of wasted edible food. Every year, significant quantities of surplus food are discarded by households, restaurants, and events, even while many people live in food insecurity. This mismatch between surplus and need has prompted communities and innovators to seek effective solutions for redirecting food that would otherwise go to waste.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
