431 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (Currently, food donation and redistribution efforts mostly rely on manual processes, disconnected communication channels, and paper-based record keeping. Donors interested in sharing surplus food typically have limited access to coordinated platforms, making it difficult to efficiently inform organizations or delivery personnel. Administrators face challenges in tracking donation requests, verifying food availability, and managing logistics without real-time data. Delivery agents often lack systematic approaches for organizing pickups and drop-offs, leading to delays and wastage.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
433 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (To overcome these challenges, the proposed Food Waste Management System leverages digital technology to facilitate the effective collection, management, and distribution of surplus food. The system provides distinct interfaces for donors, administrators, and delivery personnel, enabling seamless coordination among all stakeholders. By automating key processes such as donation registration, verification, and assignment of delivery tasks, the platform ensures organized and transparent workflows. Additionally, real-time status updates and database-driven workflows enhance visibility and accountability at every step.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
