/E (The system is composed of three primary user interfaces: Donors, Admins, and Delivery Agents. Donors access the platform via web browsers to register surplus food donations by providing details such as food type, quantity, and pickup schedule. Admins manage the system by authenticating users, verifying donation requests, approving submissions, and assigning delivery tasks to agents. Delivery agents view their assigned pickups and drop-offs and update status information to keep the system current. The core functional modules include Authentication, Donation Management, Delivery Assignment, Status Tracking, and Reporting. The Authentication module handles secure user login and role-based access control, ensuring that donors, admins, and delivery agents have appropriate privileges. Donation Management allows donors to submit donation requests, which admins can review and approve. Delivery Assignment enables the admin to allocate pickup and delivery tasks to agents based on availability and location considerations. The system is composed of three primary user interfaces: Donors, Admins, and Delivery Agents. Donors access the platform via web browsers to register surplus food donations by providing details such as food type, quantity, and pickup schedule. Admins manage the system by authenticating users, verifying donation requests, approving submissions, and assigning delivery tasks to agents. Delivery agents view their assigned pickups and drop-offs and update status information to keep the system current.)
