<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (The project reduces manual coordination, minimizes food spoilage, and promotes social responsibility by making food donation simple and accessible. Features such as secure authentication, donation tracking, role-based access, and responsive design enhance usability and system reliability. Overall, the successful implementation of this project highlights how technology can play a vital role in solving real-world social problems and contributes meaningfully toward sustainable food management and community welfare.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
686 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
687 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (Another promising direction is the use of AI-powered features such as demand forecasting to predict food requirements in different locations and seasons, as well as automated routing for delivery personnel to minimize time and fuel consumption. The system could also support multilingual interfaces to increase accessibility and reach a wider user base. Features like real-time notifications, mobile app integration, and analytics dashboards for NGOs and administrators would enhance usability and decision-making. With these advancements, the Food Waste Management System can evolve into a smart, scalable, and socially impactful platform that significantly contributes to sustainable food distribution and community welfare.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
